  "title": "Food",
  "description": "Learn essential Japanese words for common foods and drinks, plus how to say you want to eat and drink them.",
  "guidebook": "Welcome to the Food unit! 🍱\n\nIn this unit, you'll learn common food and drink vocabulary. Japanese nouns don't have articles like \"a\" or \"the,\" so コーヒー means both \"coffee\" and \"the coffee.\"\n\n**Wanting things** uses the verb ほしい (hoshii). To say \"I want coffee,\" say コーヒーがほしい (kōhī ga hoshii). The particle **が (ga)** marks what you want.\n\n**Eating and drinking** use 食べる (taberu, \"to eat\") and 飲む (nomu, \"to drink\"). To say \"I eat rice,\" use ごはんをたべる (gohan o taberu). The particle **を (o)** marks the direct object.\n\n**Polite form**: Adding ます (masu) makes sentences polite. のみます (nomimasu) = \"drink (polite).\"\n\n**Word order** is Subject + Object + Verb: わたしはパンをたべます (Watashi wa pan o tabemasu) = \"I eat bread.\"\n\nEnjoy your meal — itadakimasu! 🍣",
